imc-2012-10.prompt:
Let $c\ge1$ be a real number. Let $G$ be an abelian group and let $A\subset G$ be a finite set satisfying $|A+A|\le c|A|$, where $X+Y:=\{x+y\mid x\in X,\ y\in Y\}$ and $|Z|$ denotes the cardinality of $Z$. Prove that
$$|\underbrace{A+A+\dots+A}_{k\text{ times}}|\le c^k|A|$$
for every positive integer $k$. (Plünnecke's inequality)
